```c
#define STATUS_REG (*(volatile unsigned int *)0x1000)

void wait_for_status_bit() {
    while (!(STATUS_REG & 0x01)) {
        // Loop until LSB becomes 1
    }
}
```
The `volatile` keyword ensures that `STATUS_REG` is read from memory in each iteration of the `while` loop, rather than the compiler caching its value in a CPU register.
